tps://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T14:05:51-07:00","id":1143030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1140291-what-would-pennywise-be-in-a-changling-game?p=1140585#post1140585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think IT is meant to be a cosmic entity beyond mortal - or even Changeling - comprehension, with Pennywise just being a mask it wears for the sake of convenience and causing fear. So ... some sort of avatar of one of the Fomorians, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah, IT is a shapeshifter composed of pure energy. Pennywise is only one of many, many possible disguises that IT likes to assume when hunting in our world.<br /> <br /> IT's arch nemesis is a cosmic turtle who is attributed with having vomited up our universe. So, you know, he's considerably more powerful than your typical Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T14:46:51-07:00","id":1143045,"title":"","content":"A White Court Fomorian, obviously; It was one of the few Fomorians that escaped binding. It arrived in Derry millennia after the War of Trees to hunt, and has been there ever since. It has infused Its Arts so thoroughly throughout Derry that Derry may as well be an extension of Itself.<br /> <br /> However...It's not entirely immune to Banality and requires both massive doses of dark Glamour as well as lengthy periods of hibernation to maintain Its existence in the Waking World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T18:59:57-07:00","id":1143380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1140291-what-would-pennywise-be-in-a-changling-game?p=1143045#post1143045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A White Court Fomorian, obviously; It was one of the few Fomorians that escaped binding. It arrived in Derry millennia after the War of Trees to hunt, and has been there ever since. It has infused Its Arts so thoroughly throughout Derry that Derry may as well be an extension of Itself.<br /> <br /> Howev